\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 How the twittering works:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-1330\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Syllables:
\f1\b0  a 
\f2\fs26 mc.phasor~
\f1\fs24  drives each voice at its own rate: 9, 13, 7, 11, 15, 8, 12 and 10 syllables per second. A 
\f0\b rate
\f1\b0  number box scales all of them.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Air puffs:
\f1\b0  each syllable gives the jet a puff, (1\uc0\u8722 phase)\'b2 scaled to 0.3\'961. That puff multiplies your snowfall pressure before 
\f2\fs26 mc.snapshot~
\f1\fs24 , which now samples every 5 ms so the puffs come through cleanly.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Continuous:
\f1\b0  an 
\f0\b air floor
\f1\b0  number box (default 4.) sets the lowest pressure of 
\f2\fs26 mc.scale~
\f1\fs24 , so every jet keeps twittering between snowfall events. Set it to 0 and you get the old intermittent chirps back.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Pitch glides:
\f1\b0  each syllable glides down onto that voice's centre. The tube pitch goes out every 5 ms through 
\f2\fs26 mc.target
\f1\fs24  as 
\f2\fs26 setvalue N tube1_hkw@pitch f
\f1\fs24 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-1330\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Distinct per voice:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-1330\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Tonal centre:
\f1\b0  1760, 1976, 2093, 2349, 2637, 2794, 3136 and 3520 Hz (A6 to A7, all different). Voices 1\'963, which get less pressure, have the lower centres. A 
\f0\b transpose
\f1\b0  number box scales them all.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Glide depth:
\f1\b0  from 0.18 to 0.6 above the centre; 0.5 starts a fifth above.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Timbre:
\f1\b0  about 300 ms after each model build, a message box sends each voice its own settings:\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-1330\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 bore flare
\f1\b0  (
\f2\fs26 radius1
\f1\fs24 ): narrow gives a pure whistle, wide a reedier sound.\
\ls2\ilvl1
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 brightness
\f1\b0  (
\f2\fs26 freq-loss
\f1\fs24 ): low is bright, high is dull.\
\ls2\ilvl1
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 breathiness
\f1\b0  (
\f2\fs26 lab1_hkw@noise
\f1\fs24 ).\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-1330\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
